WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Take a docs site with the same authentication steps under Getting Started,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.660
Developers and API.

3
00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.767
Menus like that follow the org chart,

4
00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:11.027
so I'd build the documentation structure around reader routes,

5
00:00:11.027 --> 00:00:12.427
through setup and use,

6
00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:13.933
then failure and change.

7
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:16.653
Then I'd give authentication one canonical home,

8
00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:19.653
so the guide owns creating and rotating a key,

9
00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:22.133
and the reference owns status codes.

10
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:23.753
Before moving pages,

11
00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:27.333
I'd hand a reviewer a task like a failing webhook check,

12
00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:30.467
and rename the route if two labels look equally right.

13
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:33.807
So check that each label narrows the reader's next decision,

14
00:00:33.807 --> 00:00:37.647
because one that only shows ownership belongs in repository metadata.
